  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le Y\\le 1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{P((0\\le Y\\le 1),X=3)}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,(0\\le Y\\le 1))}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,Y=0)+P(X=3,Y=1)}{P(X=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,0)+f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.1+0+0.15 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,0)=0.1$ and $f(3,1)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0\\le Y\\le 1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,0)+f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.25} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
